            <ArticleTitle>Lethal synchronization of multivessel instability in acute coronary syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E100-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with acute coronary syndromes can display widespread coronary instability. We report a case presenting with ST segment elevation myocardial infarction and rapid progression to thrombosis of all major epicardial coronary arteries documented by angiography and at autopsy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
